{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass in the watch.</b> The alef is added." "<b>And YHWH looked.</b> The meaning is the angel of YHWH, the one previously mentioned, and likewise in the matter of Gideon, for the emissary is called by the name of the one who sent him, for after he commanded him to do so, he does it." "<b>In the pillar of fire and cloud.</b> Between the two pillars." "<b>And he threw [them] into panic.</b> It is possible that on account of this the poet said, \"The voice of your thunder in the whirlwind\" (Psalms 77:19), and similarly, \"The lightning-bolts multiplied and threw [them] into panic\" (ibid. 18:15), and in another place, \"And he threw them into panic\" (II Samuel 22:15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:29.602802413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}